        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-14T19:08:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we avoid memcpy?\nconst struct { UINT16 size; BYTE buf[4]; } TPM2_ECC_EK_NAME_CR50 \u003d { 4, { 0xc2, 0xe0, 0x31, 0x93 } };\nlocal_extra \u003d (TPM2B *)\u0026TPM2_ECC_EK_NAME_CR50;\n\n_cpri__KDFa should have taken const TPM2B* as contextU since it is an IN parameter. too bad it doesn\u0027t, and I don\u0027t want to go and change it. so, let\u0027s treat it as a legacy API and convert const TPM2B* to TPM2B* for its use.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 191,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 191,
        "endChar": 8
      },
      "revId": "d51b8ebf832adc65bfc805e12efc6bc00d4ba7db",
