      "writtenOn": "2018-11-14T19:08:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "if we don\u0027t eliminate memcpy altogether (see above), this is quite fragile: what if we change truncated_extra.b.size in the future? it\u0027s easy to forget to change this.\n\nI\u0027d actually establish some constant:\n  const size_t TRUNCATED_PERSONALIZE_EXTRA_SIZE \u003d 4;\n  \nand use it in the rest of the code:\n  BUILD_ASSERT(sizeof(TPM2_ECC_EK_NAME_CR50) \u003d\u003d TRUNCATED_PERSONALIZE_EXTRA_SIZE);\n  TPM2B_4_BYTE_VALUE truncated_extra \u003d { .t \u003d {TRUNCATED_PERSONALIZE_EXTRA_SIZE} };\n  memcpy(truncated_extra.b.buffer, TPM2_ECC_EK_NAME_CR50,\n         TRUNCATED_PERSONALIZE_EXTRA_SIZE);",
